       {
        "typeName": "dsDescription",
        "multiple": true,
        "typeClass": "compound",
        "value": [
         {
          "dsDescriptionValue": {
           "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
           "multiple": false,
           "typeClass": "primitive",
           "value": "This dataset contains the primary data and derived metrics from the parliamentary\nco-authorship network of the Spanish Second Republic (1931–1939), constructed from the\nDiarios de Sesiones del Congreso de los Diputados (Official Record of Parliamentary\nDebates).\n\nThe network connects the 1,026 deputies who served across the three constitutional\nlegislatures (1931–1933, 1933–1936, 1936–1939) through edges representing the joint\nsigning of legislative measures: bills, amendments, collective petitions, interpellations,\nand other parliamentary initiatives. Edge weight equals the number of measures co-signed\nby each deputy pair.\n\nThe dataset includes: (1) the complete record of individual co-authorships (94,621\nrecords); (2) political and territorial metadata for the 1,446 unique deputy-legislature pairs;(3) the network edge list (63,508 co-authoring pairs); (4) social network analysis\nmetrics for each deputy per legislature and for the full period, including centralities,\nGuimerà-Amaral indicators, ego-network metrics, behavioural profiles, a six-category\nstructural role taxonomy, inter-party proximity matrices, and aggregate party statistics;\nand (5) a lightweight structural role index for use in visualisations.\n\nThis is the first systematic reconstruction of the legislative collaboration networks of\nthe Spanish Second Republic. The dataset is an autonomous sub-product of the Luz y\nTaquígrafos corpus (DOI: 10.7910/DVN/THQCMI)."
          },
          "dsDescriptionDate": {
           "typeName": "dsDescriptionDate",
           "multiple": false,
           "typeClass": "primitive",
           "value": "2026-04-29"
          }
         }
        ]
